    "provenance": "Ground sheet removed before normalization. Base colour re-baked (Cycles CPU, emission, selected-to-active) from the approved TRELLIS source mesh; there is no rear-view projection, so the back, far side and underside are as TRELLIS invented them from the single approved concept. Tangent normals baked from the source geometry and whiteout-blended with colour relief; AO baked from the decimated geometry; roughness set inside declared regions (horns, hooves, the saturated collar, muzzle) and otherwise the default, both reduced by colour detail; no metal and no dye mask (the ox is never dyed; base alpha is zero and encoded losslessly). Base colour lifted by luma power toneGamma (chroma ratios kept), set by eye in review renders, not calibrated against the concept. Artistic derivation, not measured PBR."
